-- title:
--   Separability of the residue extension at a vertical height-one prime
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and a discrete valuation ring $A$ that is a domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$. Fix a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M p$. Let $K_M$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $K_N$ the corresponding field for level $M\ell$; both are $A$-algebras compatibly with $L$, and $K_M \le K_N$. Let $j_M \in K_M$ and $j_N \in K_N$ be nonzero elements whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ of $j$. Write $C_M = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_M\,j_M$ and $C_N = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_N\,j_N$ for the subalgebras of elements integral over $A[j_M]$, resp. $A[j_N]$. Let $\iota_M : C_M \to C_N$ be an $A$-algebra map acting as the identity on Laurent series, and suppose $C_N$ is a $C_M$-algebra with structure map $\iota_M$. Let $Q \subset C_N$ be a prime of height one containing the image of the maximal ideal of $A$, with the localisations at $Q$ and at its contraction $Q \cap C_M$ related by a compatible algebra structure. Then the residue field extension $\kappa(Q \cap C_M) \subseteq \kappa(Q)$ is separable.
--
--   This is the separability half of the statement that the level-raising map of integral models of $X_1$ is étale along the fibre over the residue characteristic: the unique vertical height-one prime of the finite chart corresponds to the generic point of the special fibre, so the assertion is that $\mathbb{F}_p(X_1(M\ell))$ is separable over $\mathbb{F}_p(X_1(M))$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOne.finite_and_etale_chartAlgFin_levelRaise_x1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOne.finite_and_etale_chartAlgFin_levelRaise_x1).
